invariant: INV-46
file: mlkem_vector.c
catches: mlkem_vector_equiv_test
reason: the base multiplication reads its twiddle factors four entries
  below the ones mlk_poly_basemul reads for each block of 16
  coefficients, so every pair's product is taken modulo another
  polynomial. The equivalence test finds the coefficients that differ.

--- old
        twiddle w = twiddle_of(lanes_mul_low(lanes_pairs(&MLK_ZETAS[64 + 4 * block]), signs));
--- new
        twiddle w = twiddle_of(lanes_mul_low(lanes_pairs(&MLK_ZETAS[60 + 4 * block]), signs));
